{
 "about": "The hero types of layout v4 (references/layout-v4.md section 3), each built in this folder as hero-<id>.html and shot at 1440x900, 1024x768, 820x1180 and 390x844. A builder deals one at random by the brief's type and the material it really has: node <skill>/assets/layout/deal.mjs --type <software|product|service> --has <photo,ui,film,object,ground>. A place's hero is never dealt: it is always 'place' (local-business Recipe 3, hero-place.html), and no other hero lists place. Every hero is exactly one screen (height 100svh) with the fixed header (72px, 56 on a phone) over its top: its words start 48px under the header (y 120 at 1440x900, y 96 at 390x844; 40 and 24 under a place's photograph), its content ends 64px above the fold (24 on a phone, plus the action bar), and nothing of the next section shows. Its blocks stand on the container's two lines (x 80 and 1360 at 1440, 24 and 366 at 390) or run edge to edge; never out to one viewport edge only. Nothing is laid over a photograph to make words readable (no scrim, gradient or veil: PH-31). Numbers are px, measured on the demos (check.mjs prints them): [1440x900, 390x844]. h1 sizes in 'size' are before --ly-scale; the measured ones in at1440/at390 are after the demo's scale.",
 "fields": {
  "types": "business types it may be dealt to, with weights; a type missing is never dealt. place is never dealt: deal.mjs always prints the 'place' hero for it. gaming is a kind, not a page type (a game is page type software): its weights are read by deal.mjs for a game (--kind gaming, or --type software --has film,photo without ui) and never for a software brief; no hero for a game lists ui. A game without art files passes --has setting (stand-in photographs of its setting, found with photos.mjs search) and is printed the photo hero, its name set large on the photograph's calm side; --has object (its key art rendered with assets/objects/product-render) only when the brief asks for 3D. A game never deals statement or word: an effect never replaces its key art",
  "needs": "the material it cannot do without (a|b means either): photo (a strong photograph of the real thing, at least 1920 wide for a full-bleed one: the client's own, else a stand-in found with photos.mjs search and listed in the report), ui (the client's screens or kit fragments from assets/ui rewritten to its names), film (a real film; without one the control links to the film's page, never a dead button), object (a product photograph on a plain ground, a cut-out, the client's render, or a product render composed with assets/objects/product-render when the brief asks for 3D or a render), setting (a game without art files: stand-in photographs of the place its world is set in), ground (nothing: a CSS ground from assets/backgrounds)",
  "h1": "the layout.css token, its size at 1440 and 390 before --ly-scale, the leading, the most lines at each width and the longest headline that fits",
  "grid": "where each block stands on the 12 columns at 1440 (from 1024 up); below 1024 everything stacks in the order given",
